 "notes": "Spine: need -> hypothesis -> Au core-satellite base + TMAPS/TEOS route -> DNA assembly feeds silicification -> conformal ultrathin shell -> (A) acid stability, (B) fixed gap -> reproducible SERS -> single-molecule events -> super-resolution hotspot mapping -> conclusion. FDTD enhancement (F5a,b) enters as side PRP premises for the two MEC bridges. Lost: Fig. S2/S3/S6 content (control spectra, gap statistics for core-satellite, bare R6G), numeric localisation precision (text only). F4 had no panels offered (C1_count_mismatch): cited by figure only. Audits: a1 (pH 4 red-tail rise, text-silent) and l1 (single-molecule assignment by fluctuation only). F5b shows the bare-gap EF ~80x below silicified at 2 nm while the text says 'slightly reduced' (recorded on n14).",
